From: tas0dev <156896971+tas0dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x86/mboot: bound the GPU renderer wait

Do not stall an entire desktop frame for a minute when the userspace DRM
renderer cannot start. The compositor retries GPU submission, so a short
bounded wait preserves recovery without silently forcing software rendering.
---
 arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
index eeeeeeeeeeee..ffffffffffff 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
@@ -1395,6 +1395,6 @@ static int mboot_gpu_submit(const struct mboot_control_request *request)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	waited = wait_event_interruptible_timeout(mboot_gpu_request_wait,
-		READ_ONCE(mboot_gpu_open), msecs_to_jiffies(60000));
+		READ_ONCE(mboot_gpu_open), msecs_to_jiffies(5000));
 	if (waited <= 0)
 		return waited ? waited : -ETIMEDOUT;
 	mutex_lock(&mboot_gpu_lock);
-- 
